# The Ajazz AKP03E controller for the person at this computer.
#
# Installed by the QO-100 NB and Radio .debs as
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-<package>-pad.rules (tools/build-deb.sh). Each
# package carries its own copy under its own name, so the two install side
# by side; two identical rules do no harm.
#
# Why not shack_pad's own rule (91-openhamshack-pad.rules): that one gives
# the pad to group shack-input, for the controller's input host service. On
# a desktop there is no such service and nobody is in that group; the pad
# belongs to whoever is logged in at the seat, which is what uaccess does
# (an ACL for the active session's user, dropped when they log out).
# uaccess must be tagged before 73-seat-late.rules applies it, hence 60-.
#
# Only the hidraw nodes of USB 0300:3002, the one model the apps drive.
# Both of its nodes match: input0 is the pad; input1 is its keyboard face,
# which the apps never open (shack_pad picks input0).
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0300", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3002", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
